{
  "input_checkpoint": "25b20c945e8f3857a3050d5ef39732a3846747f1",
  "verdict": "Scoped clear for the signed bending moments of the two registered half-order faces under fixed mid-surface area and separation, the reserved-curvature predictions, and the threshold separating the two incremental stiffness signs for the assumed squared-order axial modulus. The physical modulus, mixed-curvature law, rim reaction and free-mouth force remain open.",
  "independent_method": [
    "At zero curvature the symmetric strip can be cut at its middle. On the positive half the flat order c is even and its curvature derivative u is odd. With x=s/delta and p=k delta, u=dc/dp solves u_xx=(1-6c+6c^2)u-c_x with zero values at the middle, the pinned face and the outer bath. Integration by parts gives the two-face neutral derivative D/(a delta^3)=-4 integral(c_x u dx) on the positive half.",
    "The added reference energy is quadratic in axial strain. The relaxed flat axial stiffness distribution contributes the weighted second moment Y integral(s^2 c^2 ds) at first order in curvature. Reflection makes the weighted centroid zero. A general asymmetric laminate under zero axial resultant would instead use the second moment about its stiffness-weighted centroid.",
    "A separate piecewise-linear finite-element minimum of the full energy used 5, 10 and 20 elements per interface width, three-point exact integration of the element energy, and both signs of each curvature. Independent re-equilibration on either side of each curvature supplied the energy differences. Richardson extrapolation of the two finer grids is compared with the primary moment from the stress profile."
  ],
  "interpretation": [
    "Moments use the external work convention. The internal restoring moment has the opposite sign. Energy per reference three-area has units E/L^3, four-dimensional axial stress has units E/L^4, and its first thickness moment has units E/L^2, the same as end torque per transverse two-area.",
    "Both faces are held at fixed half-order heights. The fixed cylindrical test can include end tension, including the resting tension of both interfaces. The axial modulus specifies a reduced released-normal-stress response with the other tangential directions held. The single longitudinal invariant supplies no constitutive equation for shear or for independent hoop curvature.",
    "The neutral action contains only order, its gradient, and the resting carrier. The benchmark adds persistent longitudinal registry. The previous optical curl term cannot fix this wave-off modulus and a zero added modulus does not characterize every sliding multilayer. The complete neutral strip and a single side of a throat carry different interfacial energies."
  ],
